#!/bin/bash
# land-gem-checkout.sh — lock a design, find it in the sidebar, pay for all of
# them at once.
#
# BOTH SIDES (together-city-chat + together-city-react). Vercel AND Railway.
# INCLUDES A DATABASE MIGRATION — one nullable column on AstroProfile. The
# deploy runs `prisma generate` then `migrate deploy`, so it applies itself.
# PRECONDITION: land-metal-and-loose.sh.
set -euo pipefail

cd "$(dirname "$0")"
[ -d together-city-chat ] || { echo "!! Run this from the Together-Ai repo root."; exit 1; }

if [ -f .git/index.lock ] && [ ! -s .git/index.lock ]; then
  echo "== clearing a stale empty .git/index.lock"
  rm -f .git/index.lock
fi

NEEDS="A locked commission has to be waiting somewhere"
LOG="$(git log --oneline -40)"
case "$LOG" in
  *"$NEEDS"*) echo "== \"$NEEDS\" is already here. Nothing to do."; exit 0 ;;
esac
case "$LOG" in
  *"A gold price goes stale in a day"*) ;;
  *) echo "!! Run land-metal-and-loose.sh first — this is written against the tree it produces."; exit 1 ;;
esac

ALLOWED='^ M together-city-react/(public/assets/img/(apple-touch-icon-180|tc-icon-1024|tc-icon-192|tc-icon-512|tc-icon-maskable-512)\.png|public/downloads/TogetherCity\.apk)$'
DIRTY="$(git status --porcelain \
  | grep -Ev '^\?\? (land-.*\.sh|push-.*\.sh|.*\.patch)$' \
  | grep -Ev "$ALLOWED" || true)"
if [ -n "$DIRTY" ]; then
  echo "!! The tree carries changes this script did not expect:"; echo "$DIRTY"; exit 1
fi

PATCH="$(mktemp "${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/land.XXXXXX")"
trap 'rm -f "$PATCH"' EXIT
cat <<'B64EOF' | tr -d '\n' | openssl base64 -d -A > "$PATCH"

B64EOF
WANT="486376299761a79a90f9c9b92b5baef41bb0f8562f0dcdf8c37324c8740b79fc"
GOT="$(shasum -a 256 "$PATCH" | awk '{print $1}')"
[ "$GOT" = "$WANT" ] || { echo "!! Patch is corrupt."; echo "   want $WANT"; echo "   got  $GOT"; exit 1; }
echo "== patch verified"
git apply --check -C1 "$PATCH" || { echo "!! Patch does not apply cleanly. Nothing written."; exit 1; }
git apply -C1 "$PATCH"
echo "== applied — including one migration"

echo "== gates: the API"
cd together-city-chat
npx tsc --noEmit
npx jest src/astrology
cd ..

echo "== gates: the web app"
cd together-city-react
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run
node scripts/a11y-audit.mjs
node scripts/motion-ceiling.mjs
node scripts/lint-ceiling.mjs
npx vite build
cd ..

git add together-city-chat/prisma together-city-chat/src/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/features/astrology \
        together-city-react/src/app/router.tsx \
        together-city-react/src/app/one-stone-answer.test.ts \
        together-city-react/src/config/hubs.ts \
        together-city-react/src/styles/layout.css
git commit -F - <<'MSG'
A locked commission has to be waiting somewhere

The studio priced a stone properly and then had nowhere to put it. "Look at the
others" threw the whole configuration away — the cut, the mount, the metal, the
size, the grade, all of it — and there was no cart, no door in the menu, and no
way to buy two stones in one go.

LOCKING IS FREE AND BOTH BUTTONS DO IT. "Lock this and see the others" holds the
design and goes back to the list; "Commission this stone" is the same lock with
the checkout on the end of it. So somebody who wants one stone never meets a
cart they did not ask for, and somebody choosing three does not pay three
separate times. Nothing is charged in the studio at all now: that page decides
WHAT is being made, and the checkout decides what is being paid for.

CHECKOUT IS THE SIXTH THING IN THE SIDEBAR, because a cart you can only reach
from the page you just left is not a cart.

THE PAGE IS A SHOP CHECKOUT, WHICH IS A LAYOUT RATHER THAN A SKIN. The order on
the left, one line per commission with its photograph, its full specification,
the stone and the metal shown separately and a way to remove it; the summary on
the right, stuck to the top of the screen while the list scrolls — subtotal,
total, one button, nothing else on the page to wander off through. That
structure is borrowed because everybody has already learned it. The material
stays the city's: no second typeface, no second palette. The thing being bought
is an 84,000 commission from an astrology hub and it should not suddenly look
like a t-shirt store.

A COMMISSION IS NOT A PRODUCT ID, so a line is the whole configuration and the
studio is the only thing that makes one. Nothing stored is a price: the gem
rate, the gold rate, the weight model and the making charge all live in files on
the server, and a cart carrying its own totals would check out at a number the
shop no longer offers — with gold moving daily, that is not a hypothetical.
Every figure is recomputed on every read from the same code the studio quoted
from, and again at the charge, and the request carries no amount.

One line per stone: designing a ruby ring, going back and designing it again is
somebody changing their mind, not ordering two — and two rubies for one Sun is
not something the tradition would recognise either.

A cart that cannot be priced says why. The carats come from body weight, so
without one the lines exist and cannot be costed, which is a different thing
from an empty cart and reads differently on the page.

THE MIGRATION IS ONE NULLABLE COLUMN on AstroProfile — JSON, exactly as the
Beauty hub's bag lives in BeautyProfile.extras, because columns for cut, mount,
metal, size and grade would be a migration per design decision. It is read and
written with raw SQL and that is a DATED EXCEPTION with the reason written at
the call site: the generated client in the workspace this was built in predates
the column, and the sandbox cannot reach Prisma's engine CDN to regenerate. Raw
SQL needs no generated types, so the two statements are covered by tests today
rather than waiting for an environment. The deploy runs `prisma generate` before
the build, so after this lands they can be swapped for typed access with nothing
else changing — everything either side of them already speaks in GemCartLine[].
MSG

echo "== committed"
cat <<'DONE'

===============================================================
 Landed: A locked commission has to be waiting somewhere
 Push. Railway runs prisma generate -> build -> migrate deploy,
 so the new column applies itself. Then:
   Astrology -> Gemstones -> Add to cart -> Lock -> Checkout
===============================================================

DONE
